      "text": "**Not clearly.** The latest city-level readings show unhealthy air in both places: Singapore’s central-area PM2.5 was **187 µg/m³** at 4 p.m. on **October 17**, while Johor Bahru’s Larkin monitoring station showed a Malaysian API of **175**. Those are different measures, so they don’t support a precise apples-to-apples comparison. ([asiahaze.com](https://asiahaze.com/))\n\nJohor has worse pockets nearby—Pasir Gudang was at **API 198**—but based on the readings available, I can’t say Johor Bahru itself is worse than Singapore right now. ([semakapi.my](https://semakapi.my/en))",
